Z||000000||DerekD||04-16-2001||02:22 PM|||| Just curious if anyone might have some detailed information about removing the sail panels on an 87 GT.<P>------------------<BR>Drive It Like You Stole IT !||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-16-2001||02:35 PM||||there is a string installed at the factory. IF you can find the fishing line looking string just pull it and out comes the window intact and not mess to clean up.. i had to take the inside fiberglas piece out and smack the window with a hammer.. it's plastic so it wasn't really messy just a pain... i replaced them with units from the Fierowarehouse<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrant.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrant.jpg</A> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">       <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.epdyno.com" TARGET=_blank>www.epdyno.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.enthuzacar.com" TARGET=_blank>www.enthuzacar.com</A> <P><BR>oh yeah .. welcome to the forum!!! <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||04-16-2001||02:57 PM||||If you get them out using the "fishing line", good for you. I tried it but the line just snapped. I wound up busting them all up and removing them in pieces. Clean up was tough, too. But others on the list have had better luck using the product called "Goof Off" (or something similar) to remove the glue.<P>The good news is that installation is a snap.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000003||DerekD||04-16-2001||02:59 PM||||Thanks for the information, but now i have another question for you, I took peek at im guessing your fiero there with the blacked out sail panels. Would that be tint or something u had custom made ?<P>------------------<BR>Drive It Like You Stole IT !||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||04-16-2001||03:38 PM||||Doug at Fierowarehouse makes timted versions. The tint is actually in the plastic. Tinting with film would be problematic, but not totally impossible I suppose. But if memory serves me, the tinted versions are the same price.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DerekD||04-16-2001||03:49 PM||||Thanks for information Stimpy. Any chance you have a URL for the Fiero Warehouse.<P>------------------<BR>Drive It Like You Stole IT !||||reg||6
Z||000006||Cameron||04-16-2001||03:54 PM||||I have heard that a cable like the ones used for brakes on a bicycle. using the fishing line method...you can not only move it and it won't break but you can also saw with it alittle bit, aslong as you do it carefully as not to cut the plastic.  good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
